; io — the console, at the only two types every host agrees on.
;
; See `lib/io/go.oro` for what this module is and why it has no prefix, and
; `os.oro` in this directory for the naming rule itself.
;
; `console.log` of a JavaScript number prints its decimal digits for every value
; inside ADR 0012's window; above 1e21 it switches to exponential, which is
; outside the window and outside the claim. The one hazard this host has here is
; NEGATIVE ZERO — `console.log(-0)` prints `-0` where the other three print `0` —
; and it cannot arise, because `idiv` and `irem` normalise it at the source
; (integers.md §0a) rather than every consumer having to know.

(provides js io
    (prim print-line ((s string)) string stmt "console.log(%s)")
    ; ---- and the same without the newline
    ;
    ; `process.stdout.write`, not `console.log`, and it is the ONE place this
    ; module reaches past the console: `console.log` appends a newline and has no
    ; form that does not. `process` is a Node global, so this needs no import.
    (prim print ((s string)) string stmt "process.stdout.write(%s)")

    (prim print-int ((n int)) int stmt "console.log(%s)"))
